# act-local-CI compatibility config (read automatically by `act`; GitHub Actions
# never reads this file, so it has zero effect on real CI). See the global
# pre-push hook (installed via git's init.templateDir) for how/why `act push`
# runs on every push to a protected branch.
#
# Works around a real `act` bug (nektos/act#107), not anything in this repo's
# workflows: on this container-architecture=linux/amd64 job (forced by the
# pre-push hook to match GitHub's x86_64 hosted runners, since this host is
# Apple Silicon), act's bundled/toolcache `node` starts out correctly on PATH
# at `.../node/<ver>/x64/bin`. But the FIRST workflow-command `::add-path::`
# call in the job (actions/setup-python@v5's Main step, which calls it twice
# for its Python install dirs) makes act regenerate PATH for every later
# `docker exec` in the job -- and it substitutes the HOST's native arch
# (arm64 on this Apple Silicon machine) for that toolcache entry instead of
# the target container arch. `.../node/<ver>/arm64/bin` does not exist in the
# linux/amd64 image (verified: only an `x64` subfolder exists per node
# version), so every later bare `node` invocation 404s with exit 127 --
# including act's OWN internal `docker exec cmd=[node ...]` calls used to run
# later JS-based actions' Main/Post steps, not just user `run:` steps. Empirically
# confirmed in this repo's environment 2026-08-12: this one line fixes
# `Post actions/setup-python@v5` (ci.yml) under `act push
# --container-architecture linux/amd64`.
#
# --env forces PATH for the whole job, so it's still in effect (and still
# correct) after any later add-path call. The value must stay the ARCH-CORRECT
# (x64) toolcache node dir baked into the `catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest`
# image this repo's (global, machine-level) ~/.actrc selects for `ubuntu-latest`
# -- re-derive it via `docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64
# catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest cat /etc/environment` if the image (and its
# bundled node version) is ever bumped; a stale value fails loudly (127 again),
# not silently.
--env PATH=/opt/acttoolcache/node/24.19.0/x64/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/games:/usr/local/games:/snap/bin
